			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				255,
				15
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Expand workbench service exposure and add config/storage overlays\n\nAdd 21 new service handles to ExposeWorkbenchAccessor for Wind consumption:\nConfiguration, Storage, Lifecycle, Theme, WorkbenchTheme, Keybinding,\nNotification, File, Dialog, FileDialog, Clipboard, ContextKey, Host,\nExtension, Workspace, Product, Progress, Editor, EditorGroups, TextFile,\nActivity, Title, PaneComposite, ViewDescriptor, Layout.\n\nAdd two new transforms enabling Wind to inject runtime overrides without\ndisk persistence:\n- InjectConfigurationOverlay: consults `globalThis.__CEL_OVERRIDE_CONFIG__`\n  before upstream's default→user→workspace→folder chain in\n  IConfigurationService.getValue(). Bag is opt-in; unset preserves\n  upstream behavior.\n- InjectStorageOverlay: consults `globalThis.__CEL_OVERRIDE_STORAGE__` on\n  every AbstractStorageService.{get,getBoolean,getNumber,getObject} call.\n  Composite key `<scope>:<key>` disambiguates across\n  APPLICATION/PROFILE/WORKSPACE scopes.\n\nOther changes:\n- RewriteWorkerURLs: generalize pattern from specific file paths to\n  `*WorkerMain.ts` / `*Iframe.html` glob so future worker types are\n  covered automatically. Also handle `.ts`→`.js` suffix mapping.\n- StaticToDynamicImport: skip rewrite when `Pack` env var is set (bundled\n  profiles), since Vite needs static imports to walk the graph for CSS\n  extraction and tree-shaking.\n- ESBuild: add `.css` to copy-loader to avoid esbuild's default CSS\n  parser silently dropping modern syntax (@property, container queries).",
			"SHA": "b20d23f9eed8c644fca5b50dc734a87d1fb03f53"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T03:48:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⣿⡟⠀",
				251,
				187
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Switch from esbuild transform to byte-copy for VS Code sources\n\nChange VSCode.ts ESBuild config to use `loader: { \".js\": \"copy\" }` instead of parsing/transforming VS Code's `out/` tree. This byte-copies .js/.cjs/.mjs files directly to Target/, preserving tsc's original identifiers and formatting.\n\nWhy:\n- Output's Transform plugins (ExposeWorkbenchAccessor, InjectWorkerBootstrapShim, RewriteNestedWorkerBootstrap, etc.) are keyed on specific string patterns from VS Code's un-minified output\n- Previously esbuild's default minification + quote-rewriting silently no-oped every transform: the patterns never matched, and the workbench bootstrap crashed with `Unexpected token '<'` (404 HTML served as JS)\n- The `keepNames: false` + `minify: false` belt-and-suspenders ensure any future non-copied JS files also bypass mangling\n\nImpact:\n- Bundle profile: Sky's downstream Vite/Rollup re-mangles for bundled-electron production\n- Unbundled profile: `Static/Application/` serves readable identifiers (gzip-compressed, debuggable)\n- Transform plugins updated to match single-quoted form in tsc's original emit",
			"SHA": "41381d88b50a83b655c0083b5360b790289a6f02"
		},
